1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:07,288
ADP tells you what the room usually does.
OverADP tells you who your roster should draft right now.

2
00:00:07,938 --> 00:00:22,390
OverADP combines projections, ADP price, value above replacement,
uncertainty, and roster fit—then recalculates as every pick changes the board.

3
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:31,892
Target Intel identifies the best available target, explains why he fits,
and flags when a player probably won't make it back.

4
00:00:32,542 --> 00:00:42,483
Make your pick, and the recommendation changes with your starter needs,
positional scarcity, flex path, and next-turn availability.

5
00:00:43,133 --> 00:00:56,739
Our study intentionally excluded waivers, trades, lineup changes, and other in-season management.
We froze the Week One lineup to isolate the quality of the draft itself.

6
00:00:57,389 --> 00:01:11,861
Across 1,000 paired historical drafts, Target Intel produced a 50.6% top-three rate,
versus 25.7% for ADP-first teams—nearly double.

